1
00:00:13,343 --> 00:00:14,954
Okay, where was I?
/o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ wˌɛ‍ɹ wʌz ˈa‍ɪ/

2
00:00:15,031 --> 00:00:16,433
You were telling us how you met Mom.
/juː wɜː tˈɛlɪŋ ˌʌs hˌa‍ʊ juː mˈɛt mˈɑːm/

3
00:00:16,495 --> 00:00:18,296
In excruciating detail.
/ɪn ɛkskɹˈuːʃɪˌe‍ɪɾɪŋ diːtˈe‍ɪl/

4
00:00:18,416 --> 00:00:24,042
Right. So, back in 2005, when I was 27, my two best friends got engaged,
/ɹˈa‍ɪt sˈo‍ʊ bˈæk ɪn tˈuː θˈa‍ʊzənd fˈa‍ɪv wˌɛn a‍ɪ wʌz twˈɛnti sˈɛvən ma‍ɪ tˈuː bˈɛst fɹˈɛndz ɡɑːt ɛnɡˈe‍ɪd‍ʒd/

5
00:00:24,129 --> 00:00:26,751
and it got me thinking, maybe I should get married.
/ænd ɪt ɡɑːt mˌiː θˈɪŋkɪŋ mˈe‍ɪbiː a‍ɪ ʃˌʊd ɡɛt mˈæɹid/

6
00:00:26,878 --> 00:00:28,737
And then I saw Robin.
/ænd ðˈɛn a‍ɪ sˈɔː ɹˈɑːbɪn/

7
00:00:29,064 --> 00:00:30,632
She was incredible.
/ʃiː wʌz ɪnkɹˈɛdɪbə‍l/

8
00:00:30,709 --> 00:00:32,459
I just knew I had to meet her.
/a‍ɪ d‍ʒˈʌst nˈuː a‍ɪ hædtə mˈiːt hɜː/

9
00:00:32,573 --> 00:00:34,504
That's where your Uncle Barney came in.
/ðæts wˌɛ‍ɹ jʊɹ ˈʌŋkə‍l bˈɑː‍ɹni kˈe‍ɪm ˈɪn/

10
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:37,968
I suggest we play a little game I like to call "Have you met Ted?"
/a‍ɪ səd‍ʒˈɛst wiː plˈe‍ɪ ɐ lˈɪɾə‍l ɡˈe‍ɪm a‍ɪ lˈa‍ɪk tə kˈɔːl hæv juː mˈɛt tˈɛd/

11
00:00:38,044 --> 00:00:39,770
Wait, no, no, no. We're not playing "Have you met Ted?"
/wˈe‍ɪt nˈo‍ʊ nˈo‍ʊ nˈo‍ʊ wɪ‍ɹ nˌɑːt plˈe‍ɪɪŋ hæv juː mˈɛt tˈɛd/

12
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,382
Hi. Have you met Ted?
/hˈa‍ɪ hæv juː mˈɛt tˈɛd/

13
00:00:42,916 --> 00:00:44,297
So I asked her out.
/sˌo‍ʊ a‍ɪ ˈæskt hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt/

14
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:47,011
And I know this sound crazy, but after just one date,
/ænd a‍ɪ nˈo‍ʊ ðɪs sˈa‍ʊnd kɹˈe‍ɪzi bˌʌt ˈæftɚ d‍ʒˈʌst wˈʌn dˈe‍ɪt/

15
00:00:47,104 --> 00:00:50,194
I was in love with her which made me say something stupid.
/a‍ɪ wʌz ɪn lˈʌv wɪð hɜː wˌɪt‍ʃ mˌe‍ɪd mˌiː sˈe‍ɪ sˈʌmθɪŋ stˈuːpɪd/

16
00:00:50,287 --> 00:00:51,813
I think I'm in love with you.
/a‍ɪ θˈɪŋk a‍ɪm ɪn lˈʌv wɪð juː/

17
00:00:51,894 --> 00:00:52,729
What?!
/wˈʌt/

18
00:00:52,822 --> 00:00:53,983
Oh, Dad.
/ˈo‍ʊ dˈæd/

19
00:00:54,859 --> 00:00:56,390
So then what happened?
/sˌo‍ʊ ðˈɛn wʌt hˈæpənd/

20
00:00:56,913 --> 00:00:58,000
Nothing.
/nˈʌθɪŋ/

21
00:00:58,243 --> 00:01:00,616
I mean, I'd made a complete fool of myself.
/a‍ɪ mˈiːn a‍ɪd mˌe‍ɪd ɐ kəmplˈiːt fˈuːl ʌv ma‍ɪsˈɛlf/

22
00:01:00,773 --> 00:01:03,839
So, a week went by, and I decided not to call her.
/sˈo‍ʊ ɐ wˈiːk wɛnt bˈa‍ɪ ænd a‍ɪ dᵻsˈa‍ɪdᵻd nˌɑːt tə kˈɔːl hɜː/

23
00:01:03,907 --> 00:01:05,396
So you're not gonna call her?
/sˌo‍ʊ jʊ‍ɹ nˌɑːt ɡˌənə kˈɔːl hɜː/

24
00:01:05,473 --> 00:01:08,387
You went from, "I think I'm in love with you" to "I'm not gonna call her"?
/juː wˈɛnt fɹʌm a‍ɪ θˈɪŋk a‍ɪm ɪn lˈʌv wɪð juː tʊ a‍ɪm nˌɑːt ɡˌənə kˈɔːl hɜː/

25
00:01:08,459 --> 00:01:09,723
I wasn't in love with her, okay?
/a‍ɪ wˈʌzn̩t ɪn lˈʌv wɪð hɜː o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ/

26
00:01:09,789 --> 00:01:13,180
I was briefly in love with the abstract concept of getting married.
/a‍ɪ wʌz bɹˈiːfli ɪn lˈʌv wɪððɪ ˈæbstɹækt kˈɑːnsɛpt ʌv ɡˌɛɾɪŋ mˈæɹid/

27
00:01:13,242 --> 00:01:15,292
It had absolutely nothing to do with Robin.
/ɪt hæd ˌæbsəlˈuːtli nˈʌθɪŋ tə dˈuː wɪð ɹˈɑːbɪn/

28
00:01:15,918 --> 00:01:17,209
- Robin.
- Hi.

29
00:01:17,291 --> 00:01:18,636
Look who I ran into.
/lˈʊk hˌuː a‍ɪ ɹˈæn ˌɪntʊ/

30
00:01:18,712 --> 00:01:20,225
Since when do you guys know each other?
/sˈɪns wɛn dˈuː juː ɡˈa‍ɪz nˈo‍ʊ ˈiːt‍ʃ ˈʌðɚ/

31
00:01:20,291 --> 00:01:22,543
Oh, since about... here.
/ˈo‍ʊ sˈɪns ɐbˈa‍ʊt hˈɪ‍ɹ/

32
00:01:23,183 --> 00:01:25,406
Lily recognized me from the news and...
/lˈɪli ɹˈɛkəɡnˌa‍ɪzd mˌiː fɹʌmðə nˈuːz ænd/

33
00:01:25,615 --> 00:01:26,961
Hello, sailor!
/həlˈo‍ʊ sˈe‍ɪlɚ/

34
00:01:27,079 --> 00:01:28,478
They just got engaged.
/ðe‍ɪ d‍ʒˈʌst ɡɑːt ɛnɡˈe‍ɪd‍ʒd/

35
00:01:29,849 --> 00:01:31,903
Well, I should get back to the station.
/wˈɛl a‍ɪ ʃˌʊd ɡɛt bˈæk tə ðə stˈe‍ɪʃən/

36
00:01:32,153 --> 00:01:33,470
See you, guys.
/sˈiː juː ɡˈa‍ɪz/

37
00:01:35,168 --> 00:01:37,453
- Nice seeing you, Ted.
- Yeah, you, too.

38
00:01:39,818 --> 00:01:40,940
- Dawn it!
- What?

39
00:01:40,997 --> 00:01:43,459
- I'm in love with her.
- No!

40
00:01:43,811 --> 00:01:46,340
As your sponsor, I will not let you relapse.
/æz jʊ‍ɹ spˈɑːnsɚ a‍ɪ wɪl nˌɑːt lˈɛt juː ɹɪlˈæps/

41
00:01:46,403 --> 00:01:47,791
You blew it, it's over, move on.
/juː blˈuː ɪt ɪts ˈo‍ʊvɚ mˈuːv ˈɑːn/

42
00:01:47,877 --> 00:01:52,445
I don't know, I just have this feeling she's the future Mrs. Ted Mosby.
/a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt nˈo‍ʊ a‍ɪ d‍ʒˈʌst hæv ðɪs fˈiːlɪŋ ʃiːz ðə fjˈuːt‍ʃɚ mˈɪsɪz tˈɛd mˈɑːsbi/

43
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:55,460
Lily, you squeaked?
/lˈɪli juː skwˈiːkt/

44
00:01:55,685 --> 00:01:57,165
She said something about me, didn't she?
/ʃiː sˈɛd sˈʌmθɪŋ ɐbˈa‍ʊt mˌiː dˈɪdnt ʃiː/

45
00:01:57,243 --> 00:01:58,875
Come on, spill it, Red!
/kˈʌm ˈɑːn spˈɪl ɪt ɹˈɛd/

46
00:01:59,002 --> 00:02:00,006
Fine.
/fˈa‍ɪn/

47
00:02:00,114 --> 00:02:02,208
So, what do we think of Ted?
/sˈo‍ʊ wˌʌt dˈuː wiː θˈɪŋk ʌv tˈɛd/

48
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,751
Ted's something else.
/tˈɛdz sˈʌmθɪŋ ˈɛls/

49
00:02:05,848 --> 00:02:06,794
Huh.
/hˈʌ/

50
00:02:06,904 --> 00:02:08,377
I'm gonna spin that as good.
/a‍ɪm ɡˌənə spˈɪn ðæt æz ɡˈʊd/

51
00:02:08,471 --> 00:02:11,022
Lots of guys are something, I'm something else.
/lˈɑːts ʌv ɡˈa‍ɪz ɑː‍ɹ sˈʌmθɪŋ a‍ɪm sˈʌmθɪŋ ˈɛls/

52
00:02:11,104 --> 00:02:12,750
Comes on a little strong.
/kˈʌmz ˌɑːn ɐ lˈɪɾə‍l stɹˈɔŋ/

53
00:02:12,812 --> 00:02:15,249
But, that's part of my charm.
/bˈʌt ðæts pˈɑː‍ɹt ʌv ma‍ɪ t‍ʃˈɑː‍ɹm/

54
00:02:15,326 --> 00:02:17,092
But, that's part of his charm.
/bˈʌt ðæts pˈɑː‍ɹt ʌv hɪz t‍ʃˈɑː‍ɹm/

55
00:02:17,164 --> 00:02:19,490
Oh, totally. I mean, he's sweet, he's charming,
/ˈo‍ʊ tˈo‍ʊɾə‍li a‍ɪ mˈiːn hiːz swˈiːt hiːz t‍ʃˈɑː‍ɹmɪŋ/

56
00:02:19,549 --> 00:02:22,764
he's just looking for something a little bit more serious than I am.
/hiːz d‍ʒˈʌst lˈʊkɪŋ fɔː‍ɹ sˈʌmθɪŋ ɐ lˈɪɾə‍l bˈɪt mˈoː‍ɹ sˈi‍əɹɪəs ðɐn a‍ɪˈæm/

57
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:25,607
I mean, the most I can handle right now is something casual.
/a‍ɪ mˈiːn ðə mˈo‍ʊst a‍ɪ kæn hˈændə‍l ɹˈa‍ɪt nˈa‍ʊ ɪz sˈʌmθɪŋ kˈæʒuːə‍l/

58
00:02:26,278 --> 00:02:28,121
This just stays between us, right?
/ðɪs d‍ʒˈʌst stˈe‍ɪz bɪtwˈiːn ˌʌs ɹˈa‍ɪt/

59
00:02:28,187 --> 00:02:29,330
Are you kidding?
/ɑː‍ɹ juː kˈɪdɪŋ/

60
00:02:29,416 --> 00:02:31,879
This flapper? Fort Knox.
/ðɪs flˈæpɚ fˈɔː‍ɹt nˈɑːks/

61
00:02:32,467 --> 00:02:33,497
Oops.
/ˈuːps/

62
00:02:34,208 --> 00:02:35,683
She wants casual.
/ʃiː wˈɑːnts kˈæʒuːə‍l/

63
00:02:35,929 --> 00:02:38,060
Okay, I'll be casual.
/o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ a‍ɪl biː kˈæʒuːə‍l/

64
00:02:38,155 --> 00:02:41,121
I'm going to be a mushroom cloud of casual.
/a‍ɪm ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ təbi ɐ mˈʌʃɹuːm klˈa‍ʊd ʌv kˈæʒuːə‍l/

65
00:02:41,223 --> 00:02:42,196
You know why?
/juː nˈo‍ʊ wˈa‍ɪ/

66
00:02:42,297 --> 00:02:43,450
Cause it's a game--
/kˈɔːz ɪts ɐ ɡˈe‍ɪm/

67
00:02:43,522 --> 00:02:46,195
I want her to skip to the end and do the whole happily-ever-after thing.
/a‍ɪ wˈɑːnt hɜː tə skˈɪp tə ðɪ ˈɛnd ænd dˈuː ðə hˈo‍ʊl hˈæpɪlɪˈɛvɚɹˈæftɚ θˈɪŋ/

68
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:48,878
But you don't get there unless you play the game.
/bˌʌt juː dˈo‍ʊnt ɡɛt ðɛɹ ʌnlˈɛs juː plˈe‍ɪ ðə ɡˈe‍ɪm/

69
00:02:48,946 --> 00:02:50,245
So, are you going to ask her out?
/sˈo‍ʊ ɑː‍ɹ juː ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ tʊ ˈæsk hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt/

70
00:02:50,317 --> 00:02:51,718
Yeah... No!
/jˈɛh nˈo‍ʊ/

71
00:02:51,806 --> 00:02:55,610
I can't ask her out, because if I ask her out, I'm asking her out.
/a‍ɪ kˈænt ˈæsk hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt bɪkˈʌz ɪf a‍ɪ ˈæsk hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt a‍ɪm ˈæskɪŋ hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt/

72
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:59,476
So, how do I ask her out without asking her out?
/sˈo‍ʊ hˌa‍ʊ dˈuː a‍ɪ ˈæsk hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt wɪðˌa‍ʊt ˈæskɪŋ hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt/

73
00:03:02,942 --> 00:03:04,781
Did you guys get high?
/dˈɪd juː ɡˈa‍ɪz ɡɛt hˈa‍ɪ/

74
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:06,377
I got it.
/a‍ɪ ɡˈɑːt ɪt/

75
00:03:06,449 --> 00:03:07,852
I don't ask her out.
/a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt ˈæsk hɜːɹ ˈa‍ʊt/

76
00:03:07,981 --> 00:03:11,177
I invite her to our party next Friday.
/a‍ɪ ɪnvˈa‍ɪt hɜː tʊ ˌa‍ʊɚ pˈɑː‍ɹɾi nˈɛkst fɹˈa‍ɪde‍ɪ/

77
00:03:11,262 --> 00:03:12,701
We're having a party next Friday?
/wɪ‍ɹ hˌævɪŋ ɐ pˈɑː‍ɹɾi nˈɛkst fɹˈa‍ɪde‍ɪ/

78
00:03:12,762 --> 00:03:13,893
We are now.
/wiː ɑː‍ɹ nˈa‍ʊ/

79
00:03:14,016 --> 00:03:15,050
Casual.
/kˈæʒuːə‍l/

80
00:03:15,224 --> 00:03:19,387
Yeah, cause nothing says "casual" like inviting a hundred people over just to mack on one girl.
/jˈɛh kˈɔːz nˈʌθɪŋ sˈɛz kˈæʒuːə‍l lˈa‍ɪk ɪnvˈa‍ɪɾɪŋ ɐ hˈʌndɹəd pˈiːpə‍l ˌo‍ʊvɚ d‍ʒˈʌst tə mˈæk ˌɑːn wˈʌn ɡˈɜːl/

81
00:03:19,444 --> 00:03:21,927
Oh, and Lily, that's my leg.
/ˈo‍ʊ ænd lˈɪli ðæts ma‍ɪ lˈɛɡ/

82
00:03:23,316 --> 00:03:25,999
You waited five minutes to tell me that?
/juː wˈe‍ɪɾᵻd fˈa‍ɪv mˈɪnɪts tə tˈɛl mˌiː ðˈæt/

83
00:03:27,093 --> 00:03:28,353
All right, so call her up.
/ˈɔːl ɹˈa‍ɪt sˌo‍ʊ kˈɔːl hɜːɹ ˈʌp/

84
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:30,262
No, calling's not casual.
/nˈo‍ʊ kˈɔːlɪŋz nˌɑːt kˈæʒuːə‍l/

85
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:32,122
I just got to bump into her somewhere.
/a‍ɪ d‍ʒˈʌst ɡɑːt tə bˈʌmp ˌɪntʊ hɜː sˈʌmwɛ‍ɹ/

86
00:03:32,188 --> 00:03:35,409
Now, if only I knew her schedule, I could arrange a chance encounter.
/nˈa‍ʊ ɪf ˈo‍ʊnli a‍ɪ nˈuː hɜː skˈɛd‍ʒuːl a‍ɪ kʊd ɚɹˈe‍ɪnd‍ʒ ɐ t‍ʃˈæns ɛnkˈa‍ʊntɚ/

87
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:38,998
That's great, Ted-- you'll be the most casual stalker ever.
/ðæts ɡɹˈe‍ɪt tˈɛd juːl biː ðə mˈo‍ʊst kˈæʒuːə‍l stˈɔːkɚɹ ˈɛvɚ/

88
00:03:41,839 --> 00:03:44,359
Ever since Marshall put that ring on her finger,
/ˈɛvɚ sˈɪns mˈɑː‍ɹʃə‍l pˌʊt ðæt ɹˈɪŋ ˌɑːn hɜː fˈɪŋɡɚ/

89
00:03:44,425 --> 00:03:48,668
Lily had been, well, extra affectionate.
/lˈɪli hɐdbɪn wˈɛl ˈɛkstɹə ɐfˈɛkʃənət/

90
00:03:48,806 --> 00:03:50,820
Baby, no.
/bˈe‍ɪbi nˈo‍ʊ/

91
00:03:50,896 --> 00:03:54,020
I have a 25-page paper on constitutional law due Monday.
/a‍ɪ hæv ɐ twˈɛnti fˈa‍ɪvpˈe‍ɪd‍ʒ pˈe‍ɪpɚɹ ˌɑːn kˌɑːnstɪtˈuːʃənə‍l lˈɔː dˈuː mˈʌnde‍ɪ/

92
00:03:54,077 --> 00:03:55,397
I barely started.
/a‍ɪ bˈɛ‍ɹli stˈɑː‍ɹɾᵻd/

93
00:03:55,463 --> 00:03:57,272
Hey, I'm just sitting here,
/hˈe‍ɪ a‍ɪm d‍ʒˈʌst sˈɪɾɪŋ hˈɪ‍ɹ/

94
00:03:57,650 --> 00:03:59,355
wearing my ring,
/wˈɛɹɪŋ ma‍ɪ ɹˈɪŋ/

95
00:03:59,591 --> 00:04:01,869
my beautiful ring.
/ma‍ɪ bjˈuːɾɪfə‍l ɹˈɪŋ/

96
00:04:02,943 --> 00:04:06,139
Kind of makes wearing other stuff seem wrong.
/kˈa‍ɪnd ʌv mˌe‍ɪks wˈɛɹɪŋ ˈʌðɚ stˈʌf sˈiːm ɹˈɔŋ/

97
00:04:06,554 --> 00:04:07,982
Like my shirt.
/lˈa‍ɪk ma‍ɪ ʃˈɜːt/

98
00:04:08,562 --> 00:04:11,019
Kind of don't want to wear my shirt anymore.
/kˈa‍ɪnd ʌv dˈo‍ʊnt wˈɑːnt tə wˈɛ‍ɹ ma‍ɪ ʃˈɜːt ˌɛnɪmˈoː‍ɹ/

99
00:04:12,239 --> 00:04:14,520
Or... my underwear.
/ˈɔː‍ɹ ma‍ɪ ˌʌndɚwˈɛ‍ɹ/

100
00:04:14,854 --> 00:04:17,511
That's right, I'm not wearing any.
/ðæts ɹˈa‍ɪt a‍ɪm nˌɑːt wˈɛɹɪŋ ˌɛni/

101
00:04:20,164 --> 00:04:21,561
No underwear?
/nˈo‍ʊ ˌʌndɚwˈɛ‍ɹ/

102
00:04:21,637 --> 00:04:23,532
Not even slightly.
/nˌɑːt ˈiːvən slˈa‍ɪtli/

103
00:04:23,615 --> 00:04:24,653
Guys.
/ɡˈa‍ɪz/

104
00:04:26,086 --> 00:04:27,644
Boundaries.
/bˈa‍ʊndɚɹiz/

105
00:04:29,231 --> 00:04:30,289
There she is.
/ðˈɛ‍ɹ ʃiː ɪz/

106
00:04:30,352 --> 00:04:31,187
Thanks, Bill.
/θˈæŋks bˈɪl/

107
00:04:31,294 --> 00:04:35,769
I'm reporting from the Razzle Dazzle Supermarket on 75th and Columbus...
/a‍ɪm ɹɪpˈoː‍ɹɾɪŋ fɹʌmðə ɹˈæzə‍l dˈæzə‍l sˈuːpɚmˌɑː‍ɹkɪt ˌɑːn sˈɛvənti fˈɪfθ ænd kəlˈʌmbəs/

108
00:04:35,876 --> 00:04:37,571
75th and Columbus.
/sˈɛvənti fˈɪfθ ænd kəlˈʌmbəs/

109
00:04:38,703 --> 00:04:40,023
Game on!
/ɡˈe‍ɪm ˈɑːn/

110
00:04:40,468 --> 00:04:46,188
...where four-year-old Leroy Ellenberg has climbed inside a grab-a-prize machine and gotten stuck.
/wˌɛ‍ɹ fˈoː‍ɹjˈɪɹˈo‍ʊld lˈiːɹɔ‍ɪ ˈɛlənbˌɜːɡ hɐz klˈa‍ɪmd ɪnsˈa‍ɪd ɐ ɡɹˈæbɐpɹˈa‍ɪz məʃˈiːn ænd ɡˈɑːʔn̩ stˈʌk/

111
00:04:49,331 --> 00:04:52,664
And, all in the pursuit of a stuffed, purple giraffe.
/ˈænd ˈɔːl ɪnðə pɚsˈuːt əvə stˈʌft pˈɜːpə‍l d‍ʒɪɹˈæf/

112
00:04:53,034 --> 00:04:56,161
For Metro News 1, I'm Robin Trubotsky.
/fɔː‍ɹ mˈɛtɹo‍ʊ nˈuːz wˈʌn a‍ɪm ɹˈɑːbɪn tɹuːbˈɑːtski/

113
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:57,248
We're clear.
/wɪ‍ɹ klˈɪ‍ɹ/

114
00:04:57,434 --> 00:04:58,641
Thanks, Don.
/θˈæŋks dˈɑːn/

115
00:04:59,725 --> 00:05:00,457
Ted.
/tˈɛd/

116
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,983
Robin, wow!
/ɹˈɑːbɪn wˈa‍ʊ/

117
00:05:03,093 --> 00:05:04,114
What are the odds?
/wˌʌt ɑː‍ɹ ðɪ ˈɑːdz/

118
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:05,260
What are you doing here?
/wˌʌt ɑː‍ɹ juː dˌuːɪŋ hˈɪ‍ɹ/

119
00:05:05,363 --> 00:05:08,830
Oh, you know, just, uh, shopping for, uh, dip.
/ˈo‍ʊ juː nˈo‍ʊ d‍ʒˈʌst ˈʌ ʃˈɑːpɪŋ fɔː‍ɹ ˈʌ dˈɪp/

120
00:05:08,993 --> 00:05:10,162
I love dip.
/a‍ɪ lˈʌv dˈɪp/

121
00:05:10,269 --> 00:05:13,325
I mean, I don't love dip, I like dip... as a friend, you know.
/a‍ɪ mˈiːn a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt lˈʌv dˈɪp a‍ɪ lˈa‍ɪk dˈɪp æz ɐ fɹˈɛnd juː nˈo‍ʊ/

122
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:16,801
So, uh, hey, you, uh, reporting a news story or something?
/sˈo‍ʊ ˈʌ hˈe‍ɪ jˈuː ˈʌ ɹɪpˈoː‍ɹɾɪŋ ɐ nˈuːz stˈoːɹi ɔː‍ɹ sˈʌmθɪŋ/

123
00:05:16,888 --> 00:05:18,552
Yeah, kid stuck in a crane machine.
/jˈɛh kˈɪd stˈʌk ɪn ɐ kɹˈe‍ɪn məʃˈiːn/

124
00:05:18,619 --> 00:05:20,523
How sweet of you to call it news.
/hˌa‍ʊ swˈiːt ʌv juː tə kˈɔːl ɪt nˈuːz/

125
00:05:20,602 --> 00:05:23,278
Wow. Kid in a crane machine.
/wˈa‍ʊ kˈɪd ɪn ɐ kɹˈe‍ɪn məʃˈiːn/

126
00:05:23,451 --> 00:05:25,290
You just had to have that toy, didn't you?
/juː d‍ʒˈʌst hædtə hæv ðæt tˈɔ‍ɪ dˈɪdnt juː/

127
00:05:25,356 --> 00:05:27,036
Couldn't play the game like everyone else.
/kˌʊdənt plˈe‍ɪ ðə ɡˈe‍ɪm lˈa‍ɪk ˈɛvɹɪwˌʌn ˈɛls/

128
00:05:27,113 --> 00:05:28,644
You're all sweaty!
/jʊɹ ˈɔːl swˈɛɾi/

129
00:05:29,269 --> 00:05:30,179
Cute kid.
/kjˈuːt kˈɪd/

130
00:05:30,559 --> 00:05:32,231
Um, you know, it's so funny I should run into you.
/ˈʌm juː nˈo‍ʊ ɪts sˌo‍ʊ fˈʌni a‍ɪ ʃˌʊd ɹˈʌn ˌɪntʊ juː/

131
00:05:32,293 --> 00:05:35,673
We're, uh, we're having a party next Friday, if you feel like swinging by.
/wˈɪ‍ɹ ˈʌ wɪ‍ɹ hˌævɪŋ ɐ pˈɑː‍ɹɾi nˈɛkst fɹˈa‍ɪde‍ɪ ɪf juː fˈiːl lˈa‍ɪk swˈɪŋɪŋ bˈa‍ɪ/

132
00:05:35,708 --> 00:05:37,705
But, you know, whatever.
/bˈʌt juː nˈo‍ʊ wʌtˈɛvɚ/

133
00:05:37,734 --> 00:05:39,944
Oh, I'm going back home next weekend.
/ˈo‍ʊ a‍ɪm ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ bˈæk hˈo‍ʊm nˈɛkst wˈiːkɛnd/

134
00:05:40,021 --> 00:05:41,664
It's too bad it's not tonight.
/ɪts tˈuː bˈæd ɪts nˌɑːt tənˈa‍ɪt/

135
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:43,436
It is... it's tonight.
/ɪɾ ˈɪz ɪts tənˈa‍ɪt/

136
00:05:43,502 --> 00:05:45,187
This Friday. Did I say next Friday?
/ðɪs fɹˈa‍ɪde‍ɪ dˈɪd a‍ɪ sˈe‍ɪ nˈɛkst fɹˈa‍ɪde‍ɪ/

137
00:05:45,252 --> 00:05:47,931
Sorry, I guess I've been saying next Friday all week.
/sˈɔːɹi a‍ɪ ɡˈɛs a‍ɪv bˌɪn sˈe‍ɪɪŋ nˈɛkst fɹˈa‍ɪde‍ɪ ˈɔːl wˈiːk/

138
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:50,086
But, yeah, it's tonight, the, uh, the party's tonight.
/bˈʌt jˈɛh ɪts tənˈa‍ɪt ðˈə ˈʌ ðə pˈɑː‍ɹɾiz tənˈa‍ɪt/

139
00:05:50,174 --> 00:05:52,534
But, you know, whatever.
/bˈʌt juː nˈo‍ʊ wʌtˈɛvɚ/

140
00:05:58,197 --> 00:05:59,012
Hello?
/həlˈo‍ʊ/

141
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:01,012
Hey, am I interrupting anything?
/hˈe‍ɪ æm a‍ɪ ˌɪntɚɹˈʌptɪŋ ˈɛnɪθˌɪŋ/

142
00:06:01,094 --> 00:06:03,199
No, no, I'm just writing my paper.
/nˈo‍ʊ nˈo‍ʊ a‍ɪm d‍ʒˈʌst ɹˈa‍ɪɾɪŋ ma‍ɪ pˈe‍ɪpɚ/

143
00:06:03,275 --> 00:06:04,503
Hitting the books.
/hˈɪɾɪŋ ðə bˈʊks/

144
00:06:04,612 --> 00:06:07,698
Yeah, well, you and Lily might want to put some clothes on.
/jˈɛh wˈɛl juː ænd lˈɪli mˌa‍ɪt wˈɑːnt tə pˌʊt sˌʌm klˈo‍ʊðz ˈɑːn/

145
00:06:07,893 --> 00:06:09,358
We're throwing a party in two hours.
/wɪ‍ɹ θɹˈo‍ʊɪŋ ɐ pˈɑː‍ɹɾi ɪn tˈuː ˈa‍ɪ‍ʊ‍ɹz/

146
00:06:09,424 --> 00:06:10,545
Okay, bye.
/o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ bˈa‍ɪ/

147
00:06:14,881 --> 00:06:17,284
So, Gatsby, what are you gonna do when Robin shows up?
/sˈo‍ʊ ɡˈætsbi wˌʌt ɑː‍ɹ juː ɡˌənə dˈuː wɛn ɹˈɑːbɪn ʃˈo‍ʊz ˈʌp/

148
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:20,147
Okay, I got it all planned out.
/o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ a‍ɪ ɡɑːt ɪɾ ˈɔːl plˈænd ˈa‍ʊt/

149
00:06:20,668 --> 00:06:23,638
She steps through the door-- and where's Ted?
/ʃiː stˈɛps θɹuː ðə dˈoː‍ɹ ænd wˌɛ‍ɹz tˈɛd/

150
00:06:23,708 --> 00:06:25,932
Not eagerly waiting by the door.
/nˌɑːt ˈiːɡɚli wˈe‍ɪɾɪŋ ba‍ɪ ðə dˈoː‍ɹ/

151
00:06:26,081 --> 00:06:28,354
No, I'm across the room at my drafting table,
/nˈo‍ʊ a‍ɪm əkɹˌɑːs ðə ɹˈuːm æt ma‍ɪ dɹˈæftɪŋ tˈe‍ɪbə‍l/

152
00:06:28,415 --> 00:06:32,166
showing some foxy young thing all my cool architect stuff.
/ʃˈo‍ʊɪŋ sˌʌm fˈɑːksi jˈʌŋ θˈɪŋ ˈɔːl ma‍ɪ kˈuːl ˈɑː‍ɹkɪtˌɛkt stˈʌf/

153
00:06:32,239 --> 00:06:33,913
So, Robin strolls over,
/sˈo‍ʊ ɹˈɑːbɪn stɹˈo‍ʊlz ˈo‍ʊvɚ/

154
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,297
and I casually give her one of these: "Hey, what's up?"
/ænd a‍ɪ kˈæʒuːə‍li ɡˈɪv hɜː wˈʌn ʌv ðˈiːz hˈe‍ɪ wˌʌts ˈʌp/

155
00:06:38,373 --> 00:06:42,294
She says, "Hey, nice place, et cetera, et cetera."
/ʃiː sˈɛz hˈe‍ɪ nˈa‍ɪs plˈe‍ɪs ˈɛt sˈɛɾɚɹə ˈɛt sˈɛɾɚɹə/

156
00:06:42,377 --> 00:06:43,847
And then, I say,
/ænd ðˈɛn a‍ɪ sˈe‍ɪ/

157
00:06:43,908 --> 00:06:45,649
"Well, make yourself at home."
/wˈɛl mˌe‍ɪk joː‍ɹsˈɛlf æt hˈo‍ʊm/

158
00:06:45,721 --> 00:06:48,445
And, I casually return to my conversation.
/ˈænd a‍ɪ kˈæʒuːə‍li ɹɪtˈɜːn tə ma‍ɪ kɑːnvɚsˈe‍ɪʃən/

159
00:06:48,634 --> 00:06:50,590
Then, an hour later...
/ðˈɛn ɐn ˈa‍ɪ‍ʊ‍ɹ lˈe‍ɪɾɚ/

160
00:06:51,505 --> 00:06:54,791
"Oh, you're still here?" I say, 
/ˈo‍ʊ jʊ‍ɹ stˈɪl hˈɪ‍ɹ a‍ɪ sˈe‍ɪ/

161
00:06:54,855 --> 00:06:57,799
like I don't really care, but it's a nice surprise.
/lˈa‍ɪk a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt ɹˈi‍əli kˈɛ‍ɹ bˌʌt ɪts ɐ nˈa‍ɪs sɚpɹˈa‍ɪz/

162
00:06:57,871 --> 00:06:59,620
And then, very casually:
/ænd ðˈɛn vˈɛɹi kˈæʒuːə‍li/

163
00:07:00,313 --> 00:07:02,402
"Want to see the roof?"
/wˈɑːnt tə sˈiː ðə ɹˈuːf/

164
00:07:03,610 --> 00:07:04,855
The roof!
/ðə ɹˈuːf/

165
00:07:04,910 --> 00:07:07,608
Get her up to the roof, and the roof takes care of the rest.
/ɡɛt hɜːɹ ˌʌp tə ðə ɹˈuːf ænd ðə ɹˈuːf tˈe‍ɪks kˈɛɹ ʌvðə ɹˈɛst/

166
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:09,063
What's so special about the roof?
/wˌʌts sˌo‍ʊ spˈɛʃə‍l ɐbˌa‍ʊt ðə ɹˈuːf/

167
00:07:09,149 --> 00:07:12,821
Oh, the moon, the stars, the shimmering skyline.
/ˈo‍ʊ ðə mˈuːn ðə stˈɑː‍ɹz ðə ʃˈɪmɚɹɪŋ skˈa‍ɪla‍ɪn/

168
00:07:12,882 --> 00:07:15,626
You can't not fall in love on that roof.
/juː kˈænt nˌɑːt fˈɔːl ɪn lˈʌv ˌɑːn ðæt ɹˈuːf/

169
00:07:16,714 --> 00:07:18,688
We do it up there, sometimes.
/wiː dˈuː ɪɾ ˌʌp ðˈɛ‍ɹ sˈʌmta‍ɪmz/

170
00:07:19,017 --> 00:07:20,941
Solid plan, my little friend.
/sˈɑːlɪd plˈæn ma‍ɪ lˈɪɾə‍l fɹˈɛnd/

171
00:07:21,001 --> 00:07:21,934
We're the same height.
/wɪ‍ɹ ðə sˈe‍ɪm hˈa‍ɪt/

172
00:07:21,996 --> 00:07:25,267
But, may I suggest one little modification.
/bˈʌt mˈe‍ɪ a‍ɪ səd‍ʒˈɛst wˈʌn lˈɪɾə‍l mˌɑːdɪfɪkˈe‍ɪʃən/

173
00:07:25,871 --> 00:07:29,394
That foxy young thing you were chatting up, take her up to the roof and have sex with her.
/ðæt fˈɑːksi jˈʌŋ θˈɪŋ juː wɜː t‍ʃˈæɾɪŋ ˈʌp tˈe‍ɪk hɜːɹ ˌʌp tə ðə ɹˈuːf ænd hæv sˈɛks wɪð hɜː/

174
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:31,663
- Crazy monkey style...
- That's not the plan.

175
00:07:31,739 --> 00:07:33,409
Well, it should be the plan. I mean, look at her.
/wˈɛl ɪt ʃˌʊd biː ðə plˈæn a‍ɪ mˈiːn lˈʊk æt hɜː/

176
00:07:33,464 --> 00:07:36,035
Ted, look at her. She's smoking!
/tˈɛd lˈʊk æt hɜː ʃiːz smˈo‍ʊkɪŋ/

177
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:37,719
- Thank you!
- Yeah...

178
00:07:37,776 --> 00:07:39,369
But, she's not Robin!
/bˈʌt ʃiːz nˌɑːt ɹˈɑːbɪn/

179
00:07:39,424 --> 00:07:40,622
Exactly!
/ɛɡzˈæktli/

180
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:42,174
Ted, let's rap.
/tˈɛd lˈɛts ɹˈæp/

181
00:07:42,486 --> 00:07:47,161
Statistic: At every New York party, there's always a girl who has no idea whose party she's at.
/stɐtˈɪstɪk æɾ ˈɛvɹi nˈuː jˈɔː‍ɹk pˈɑː‍ɹɾi ðɛ‍ɹz ˈɔːlwe‍ɪz ɐ ɡˈɜːl hˌuː hɐz nˈo‍ʊ a‍ɪdˈi‍ə hˌuːz pˈɑː‍ɹɾi ʃiːz æt/

182
00:07:47,202 --> 00:07:50,238
She knows no one you know, and you will never see her again.
/ʃiː nˈo‍ʊz nˈo‍ʊwˈʌn juː nˈo‍ʊ ænd juː wɪl nˈɛvɚ sˈiː hɜːɹ ɐɡˈɛn/

183
00:07:50,285 --> 00:07:54,728
Do you see where I'm going with this?
/dˈuː juː sˈiː wˌɛɹ a‍ɪm ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ wɪð ðˈɪs/

184
00:07:54,795 --> 00:07:56,469
Barney, I don't think so.
/bˈɑː‍ɹni a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt θˈɪŋk sˈo‍ʊ/

185
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,529
Scoping.
/skˈo‍ʊpɪŋ/

186
00:07:58,173 --> 00:07:59,483
Scoping.
/skˈo‍ʊpɪŋ/

187
00:07:59,818 --> 00:08:01,386
Man, you're a dork.
/mˈæn jʊɹ ɐ dˈoː‍ɹk/

188
00:08:02,152 --> 00:08:03,873
Target acquired!
/tˈɑː‍ɹɡɪt ɐkwˈa‍ɪ‍ɚd/

189
00:08:03,933 --> 00:08:07,477
Now it's time we play a little game I like to call "Have you met Ted?"
/nˈa‍ʊ ɪts tˈa‍ɪm wiː plˈe‍ɪ ɐ lˈɪɾə‍l ɡˈe‍ɪm a‍ɪ lˈa‍ɪk tə kˈɔːl hæv juː mˈɛt tˈɛd/

190
00:08:07,564 --> 00:08:08,839
Oh, come on, not this.
/ˈo‍ʊ kˈʌm ˈɑːn nˌɑːt ðˈɪs/

191
00:08:08,926 --> 00:08:10,109
Hi. Have you met Ted?
/hˈa‍ɪ hæv juː mˈɛt tˈɛd/

192
00:08:10,186 --> 00:08:10,812
No.
/nˈo‍ʊ/

193
00:08:10,898 --> 00:08:12,019
- Hi.
- Hi.

194
00:08:12,095 --> 00:08:13,950
- Do you know Marshall? Lily?
- No.

195
00:08:14,032 --> 00:08:15,905
Hmm. Do you know anyone at this party?
/hˈəm dˈuː juː nˈo‍ʊ ˈɛnɪwˌʌn æt ðɪs pˈɑː‍ɹɾi/

196
00:08:16,017 --> 00:08:17,588
I work with Carlos.
/a‍ɪ wˈɜːk wɪð kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz/

197
00:08:17,835 --> 00:08:18,808
Excuse me.
/ɛkskjˈuːs mˌiː/

198
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:20,442
Anyone know a Carlos?
/ˈɛnɪwˌʌn nˈo‍ʊ ɐ kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz/

199
00:08:20,686 --> 00:08:21,568
- No.
- No.

200
00:08:21,619 --> 00:08:23,408
On a silver platter.
/ˌɑːn ɐ sˈɪlvɚ plˈæɾɚ/

201
00:08:23,707 --> 00:08:25,514
Bon appétit.
/bˈɑːn ɐpe‍ɪtˈiːt/

202
00:08:25,607 --> 00:08:26,953
I don't think so.
/a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt θˈɪŋk sˈo‍ʊ/

203
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:29,058
Your loss, her gain.
