00:13:02,498 --> 00:13:09,206
Has anybody seen An Introduction to Contract Tort and Restitution Statutes from 1865-1923?
/hɐz ˈɛnɪbˌɑːdi sˈiːn ɐn ˌɪntɹədˈʌkʃən tə kəntɹˈækt tˈɔː‍ɹt ænd ɹɪstɪtˈuːʃən stˈæt‍ʃuːts fɹʌm wˈʌn θˈa‍ʊzənd ˈe‍ɪthˈʌndɹəd sˈɪksti fˈa‍ɪv dˈæʃ nˈa‍ɪntiːnhˈʌndɹəd twˈɛnti θɹˈiː/

309
00:13:10,482 --> 00:13:12,293
Anybody seen a big-ass book?
/ˈɛnɪbˌɑːdi sˈiːn ɐ bˈɪɡˈæs bˈʊk/

310
00:13:13,132 --> 00:13:13,856
No.
/nˈo‍ʊ/

311
00:13:14,608 --> 00:13:15,570
Hello, Barney.
/həlˈo‍ʊ bˈɑː‍ɹni/

312
00:13:16,743 --> 00:13:18,704
Of course.
/ʌv kˈoː‍ɹs/

313
00:13:20,419 --> 00:13:21,561
You look well.
/juː lˈʊk wˈɛl/

314
00:13:22,017 --> 00:13:24,083
Is it weird they invited both of us?
/ɪz ɪt wˈɪ‍ɹd ðe‍ɪ ɪnvˈa‍ɪɾᵻd bˈo‍ʊθ ʌv ˌʌs/

315
00:13:24,683 --> 00:13:26,082
Who?
/hˈuː/

316
00:13:26,845 --> 00:13:30,670
Who invited you? No one even knows who you are!
/hˌuː ɪnvˈa‍ɪɾᵻd juː nˈo‍ʊwˈʌn ˈiːvən nˈo‍ʊz hˈuː juː ɑː‍ɹ/

317
00:13:31,422 --> 00:13:33,388
I understand you're hurt, but
/a‍ɪ ˌʌndɚstˈænd jʊ‍ɹ hˈɜːt bˈʌt/

318
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:35,400
you don't have to be cruel.
/juː dˈo‍ʊnt hæv təbi kɹˈuːəl/

319
00:13:36,384 --> 00:13:37,991
Carlos was right about you.
/kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz wʌz ɹˈa‍ɪt ɐbˈa‍ʊt juː/

320
00:13:39,313 --> 00:13:41,560
Who is Carlos?!
/hˌuː ɪz kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz/

321
00:13:41,667 --> 00:13:43,459
Hey, where the hell is my...?
/hˈe‍ɪ wˌɛ‍ɹ ðə hˈɛl ɪz mˈa‍ɪ/

322
00:13:43,761 --> 00:13:44,954
Oh...!
/ˈo‍ʊ ˈɛkskləmˌe‍ɪʃən/

323
00:13:47,872 --> 00:13:48,861
Okay...
/o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ/

324
00:13:50,161 --> 00:13:55,968
An Introduction to Contract Tort and Restitution Statutes from 1865-1923
/ɐn ˌɪntɹədˈʌkʃən tə kəntɹˈækt tˈɔː‍ɹt ænd ɹɪstɪtˈuːʃən stˈæt‍ʃuːts fɹʌm wˈʌn θˈa‍ʊzənd ˈe‍ɪthˈʌndɹəd sˈɪksti fˈa‍ɪv dˈæʃ nˈa‍ɪntiːnhˈʌndɹəd twˈɛnti θɹˈiː/

325
00:13:56,054 --> 00:13:57,920
is not a coaster!
/ɪz nˌɑːɾə kˈo‍ʊstɚ/

326
00:13:58,016 --> 00:14:01,631
Ted, I'm jeopardizing my law career so you can throw not one,
/tˈɛd a‍ɪm d‍ʒˈɛpɚdˌa‍ɪzɪŋ ma‍ɪ lˈɔː kɚɹˈɪ‍ɹ sˌo‍ʊ juː kæn θɹˈo‍ʊ nˌɑːt wˌʌn/

327
00:14:01,722 --> 00:14:03,955
not two, but three parties
/nˌɑːt tˈuː bˌʌt θɹˈiː pˈɑː‍ɹɾiz/

328
00:14:04,028 --> 00:14:07,293
for some girl that you just met who's probably not even going to show up!
/fɔː‍ɹ sˌʌm ɡˈɜːl ðæt juː d‍ʒˈʌst mˈɛt hˌuːz pɹˈɑːbəbli nˌɑːt ˈiːvən ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ tə ʃˈo‍ʊ ˈʌp/

329
00:14:07,369 --> 00:14:08,773
I mean, where is she, Ted, huh?
/a‍ɪ mˈiːn wˈɛɹ ɪz ʃiː tˈɛd hˈʌ/

330
00:14:08,881 --> 00:14:10,186
Where's Robin?
/wˌɛ‍ɹz ɹˈɑːbɪn/

331
00:14:12,245 --> 00:14:13,013
Hi.
/hˈa‍ɪ/

332
00:14:13,692 --> 00:14:14,712
Hi, Ron.
/hˈa‍ɪ ɹˈɑːn/

333
00:14:23,452 --> 00:14:26,866
So, you threw all these parties for me?
/sˈo‍ʊ juː θɹˈuː ˈɔːl ðiːz pˈɑː‍ɹɾiz fɔː‍ɹ mˌiː/

334
00:14:27,154 --> 00:14:29,663
No. Oh, you thought that... no!
/nˈo‍ʊ ˈo‍ʊ juː θˈɔːt ðˈæt nˈo‍ʊ/

335
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:31,726
I... okay, yes. You got me.
/ˈa‍ɪ o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ jˈɛs juː ɡˈɑːt mˌiː/

336
00:14:31,897 --> 00:14:36,523
One of the reasons I threw these parties was so that I could introduce you
/wˈʌn ʌvðə ɹˈiːzənz a‍ɪ θɹˈuː ðiːz pˈɑː‍ɹɾiz wʌz sˌo‍ʊ ðæt a‍ɪ kʊd ˌɪntɹədˈuːs juː/

337
00:14:36,611 --> 00:14:38,976
to, um, this guy.
/tˈuː ˈʌm ðɪs ɡˈa‍ɪ/

338
00:14:39,058 --> 00:14:42,222
Uh, I figured, you know, since it didn't work out between us
/ˈʌ a‍ɪ fˈɪɡɚd juː nˈo‍ʊ sˈɪns ɪt dˈɪdnt wˈɜːk ˈa‍ʊt bɪtwˈiːn ˌʌs/

339
00:14:42,288 --> 00:14:44,112
and now we can just laugh about it...
/ænd nˈa‍ʊ wiː kæn d‍ʒˈʌst lˈæf ɐbˈa‍ʊt ɪt/

340
00:14:45,521 --> 00:14:47,749
Anyway, Robin, this is...
/ˈɛnɪwˌe‍ɪ ɹˈɑːbɪn ðɪs ˈɪz/

341
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:48,924
Carlos.
/kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz/

342
00:14:49,421 --> 00:14:51,053
- Oh!
- Oh!

343
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:56,368
She's still talking to Carlos.
/ʃiːz stˈɪl tˈɔːkɪŋ tə kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz/

344
00:14:56,850 --> 00:14:59,073
I can still win this. I-it's not over.
/a‍ɪ kæn stˈɪl wˈɪn ðˈɪs a‍ɪɪts nˌɑːt ˈo‍ʊvɚ/

345
00:14:59,168 --> 00:15:01,864
Okay, buddy. Time for the tough talk.
/o‍ʊkˈe‍ɪ bˈʌdi tˈa‍ɪm fɚðə tˈʌf tˈɔːk/

346
00:15:02,032 --> 00:15:04,807
Robin seems great, but let's look at the facts.
/ɹˈɑːbɪn sˈiːmz ɡɹˈe‍ɪt bˌʌt lˈɛts lˈʊk æt ðə fˈækts/

347
00:15:04,884 --> 00:15:06,322
You want to get married.
/juː wˈɑːnt tə ɡɛt mˈæɹid/

348
00:15:06,372 --> 00:15:10,869
And right now, there's a million women in New York looking for exactly you.
/ænd ɹˈa‍ɪt nˈa‍ʊ ðɛ‍ɹz ɐ mˈɪli‍ən wˈɪmɪn ɪn nˈuː jˈɔː‍ɹk lˈʊkɪŋ fɔːɹ ɛɡzˈæktli juː/

349
00:15:10,926 --> 00:15:12,430
But Robin ain't one of them.
/bˌʌt ɹˈɑːbɪn ˈe‍ɪnt wˈʌn ʌv ðˌɛm/

350
00:15:12,496 --> 00:15:15,159
She's not just one of them. She's the one.
/ʃiːz nˌɑːt d‍ʒˈʌst wˈʌn ʌv ðˌɛm ʃiːz ðə wˈʌn/

351
00:15:15,241 --> 00:15:18,396
Yeah, well, the one is heading up to the roof.
/jˈɛh wˈɛl ðə wˈʌn ɪz hˈɛdɪŋ ˌʌp tə ðə ɹˈuːf/

352
00:15:20,986 --> 00:15:22,424
What are you going to do?
/wˌʌt ɑː‍ɹ juː ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ tə dˈuː/

353
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:24,196
Nothing.
/nˈʌθɪŋ/

354
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:28,138
It's a game. I got to just keep playing it.
/ɪts ɐ ɡˈe‍ɪm a‍ɪ ɡɑːt tə d‍ʒˈʌst kˈiːp plˈe‍ɪɪŋ ɪt/

355
00:16:07,001 --> 00:16:07,906
Ted...
/tˈɛd/

356
00:16:07,998 --> 00:16:10,168
Hey, Carlos, can you give us a minute?
/hˈe‍ɪ kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz kæn juː ɡˈɪv ˌʌs ɐ mˈɪnɪt/

357
00:16:10,231 --> 00:16:12,282
Hey, no sweat, hombre.
/hˈe‍ɪ nˈo‍ʊ swˈɛt hˈɑːmbɚ/

358
00:16:13,001 --> 00:16:13,865
See ya.
/sˈiː jɐ/

359
00:16:17,691 --> 00:16:18,612
Robin...
/ɹˈɑːbɪn/

360
00:16:18,873 --> 00:16:21,704
look, I didn't throw this party to set you up with Carlos,
/lˈʊk a‍ɪ dˈɪdnt θɹˈo‍ʊ ðɪs pˈɑː‍ɹɾi tə sˈɛt juː ˌʌp wɪð kˈɑː‍ɹlo‍ʊz/

361
00:16:21,771 --> 00:16:23,036
or the one before that,
/ɔː‍ɹ ðə wˈʌn bɪfˌoː‍ɹ ðˈæt/

362
00:16:23,425 --> 00:16:24,827
or the one before that.
/ɔː‍ɹ ðə wˈʌn bɪfˌoː‍ɹ ðˈæt/

363
00:16:26,139 --> 00:16:28,841
I threw these parties because I wanted to see you.
/a‍ɪ θɹˈuː ðiːz pˈɑː‍ɹɾiz bɪkˈʌz a‍ɪ wˈɑːntᵻd tə sˈiː juː/

364
00:16:29,850 --> 00:16:31,340
Well, here I am.
/wˈɛl hˈɪɹ a‍ɪˈæm/

365
00:16:32,712 --> 00:16:35,728
There's something here, look, unless I'm crazy.
/ðɛ‍ɹz sˈʌmθɪŋ hˈɪ‍ɹ lˈʊk ʌnlˈɛs a‍ɪm kɹˈe‍ɪzi/

366
00:16:36,239 --> 00:16:37,919
You're not crazy.
/jʊ‍ɹ nˌɑːt kɹˈe‍ɪzi/

367
00:16:39,399 --> 00:16:41,088
I don't know, Ted.
/a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt nˈo‍ʊ tˈɛd/

368
00:16:41,141 --> 00:16:43,306
I mean, we barely know each other
/a‍ɪ mˈiːn wiː bˈɛ‍ɹli nˈo‍ʊ ˈiːt‍ʃ ˈʌðɚ/

369
00:16:43,521 --> 00:16:46,598
and you're looking at me with that look. And, it's like...
/ænd jʊ‍ɹ lˈʊkɪŋ æt mˌiː wɪð ðæt lˈʊk ˈænd ɪts lˈa‍ɪk/

370
00:16:46,722 --> 00:16:47,489
Like, like what?
/lˈa‍ɪk lˈa‍ɪk wˈʌt/

371
00:16:47,602 --> 00:16:50,509
Like, "Let's fall in love and get married
/lˈa‍ɪk lˈɛts fˈɔːl ɪn lˈʌv ænd ɡɛt mˈæɹid/

372
00:16:50,566 --> 00:16:52,941
and have kids and drive them to soccer practice."
/ænd hæv kˈɪdz ænd dɹˈa‍ɪv ðˌɛm tə sˈɑːkɚ pɹˈæktɪs/

373
00:16:53,013 --> 00:16:55,558
I'm not going to force sports on them unless they're interested.
/a‍ɪm nˌɑːt ɡˌo‍ʊɪŋ tə fˈoː‍ɹs spˈoː‍ɹts ˌɑːn ðˌɛm ʌnlˈɛs ðe‍ɪɚɹ ˈɪntɹəstᵻd/

374
00:16:57,217 --> 00:16:58,569
It's a great look.
/ɪts ɐ ɡɹˈe‍ɪt lˈʊk/

375
00:16:59,219 --> 00:17:00,749
But you're looking at the wrong girl.
/bˌʌt jʊ‍ɹ lˈʊkɪŋ æt ðə ɹˈɔŋ ɡˈɜːl/

376
00:17:00,817 --> 00:17:02,473
- No, I'm not.
- Yes, you are.

377
00:17:02,557 --> 00:17:05,168
I don't want to get married right now, maybe ever.
/a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt wˈɑːnt tə ɡɛt mˈæɹid ɹˈa‍ɪt nˈa‍ʊ mˈe‍ɪbiː ˈɛvɚ/

378
00:17:05,234 --> 00:17:11,644
And, if we got together, I'd feel like I'd either have to marry you or break your heart, and...
/ˈænd ɪf wiː ɡɑːt təɡˈɛðɚ a‍ɪd fˈiːl lˈa‍ɪk a‍ɪd ˈiːðɚ hæv tə mˈæɹi juː ɔː‍ɹ bɹˈe‍ɪk jʊ‍ɹ hˈɑː‍ɹt ˈænd/

379
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:15,326
I just couldn't do either of those things.
/a‍ɪ d‍ʒˈʌst kˌʊdənt dˈuː ˈiːðɚɹ ʌv ðo‍ʊz θˈɪŋz/

380
00:17:15,818 --> 00:17:18,399
Just like you can't turn off the way you feel.
/d‍ʒˈʌst lˈa‍ɪk juː kˈænt tˈɜːn ˈɔf ðə wˈe‍ɪ juː fˈiːl/

381
00:17:21,772 --> 00:17:22,908
Click.
/klˈɪk/

382
00:17:23,109 --> 00:17:24,634
Off. Let's make out.
/ˈɔf lˈɛts mˌe‍ɪk ˈa‍ʊt/

383
00:17:24,799 --> 00:17:25,767
What?
/wˈʌt/

384
00:17:26,559 --> 00:17:28,762
What? That was the off switch.
/wˈʌt ðæt wʌzðɪ ˈɔf swˈɪt‍ʃ/

385
00:17:28,966 --> 00:17:30,353
And I turned it off.
/ænd a‍ɪ tˈɜːnd ɪɾ ˈɔf/

386
00:17:30,559 --> 00:17:34,583
I mean, look, sure, yes, I want to fall in love, get married, blah, blah, blah.
/a‍ɪ mˈiːn lˈʊk ʃˈʊ‍ɹ jˈɛs a‍ɪ wˈɑːnt tə fˈɔːl ɪn lˈʌv ɡɛt mˈæɹid blˈɑː blˈɑː blˈɑː/

387
00:17:34,650 --> 00:17:38,858
But, on the other hand... you, me,
/bˈʌt ɑːnðɪ ˈʌðɚ hˈænd jˈuː mˈiː/

388
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,926
the roof.
/ðə ɹˈuːf/

389
00:17:42,268 --> 00:17:43,820
There's no off switch.
/ðɛ‍ɹz nˈo‍ʊ ˈɔf swˈɪt‍ʃ/

390
00:17:44,732 --> 00:17:46,322
There is an off switch.
/ðɛɹ ɪz ɐn ˈɔf swˈɪt‍ʃ/

391
00:17:47,136 --> 00:17:48,474
And it's off.
/ænd ɪts ˈɔf/

392
00:17:48,975 --> 00:17:50,245
No, it's not.
/nˈo‍ʊ ɪts nˈɑːt/

393
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:52,805
Yes, it is.
/jˈɛs ɪɾ ˈɪz/

394
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:54,721
No, it's not.
/nˈo‍ʊ ɪts nˈɑːt/

395
00:17:54,781 --> 00:17:57,839
Yes... it is.
/jˈɛs ɪɾ ˈɪz/

396
00:18:12,055 --> 00:18:13,362
No, it's not.
/nˈo‍ʊ ɪts nˈɑːt/

397
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:16,639
You're right. There's no off switch.
/jʊ‍ɹ ɹˈa‍ɪt ðɛ‍ɹz nˈo‍ʊ ˈɔf swˈɪt‍ʃ/

398
00:18:17,995 --> 00:18:20,111
God, I wish there was an off switch!
/ɡˈɑːd a‍ɪ wˈɪʃ ðɛ‍ɹwˌʌz ɐn ˈɔf swˈɪt‍ʃ/

399
00:18:20,883 --> 00:18:22,170
Me, too.
/mˈiː tˈuː/

400
00:18:27,489 --> 00:18:29,412
So, um...
/sˈo‍ʊ ˈʌm/

401
00:18:30,694 --> 00:18:32,244
What do we do now?
/wˌʌt dˈuː wiː dˈuː nˈa‍ʊ/

402
00:18:34,964 --> 00:18:36,356
We could be friends.
/wiː kʊd biː fɹˈɛndz/

403
00:18:36,627 --> 00:18:37,831
Oh...
/ˈo‍ʊ/

404
00:18:39,208 --> 00:18:43,924
Look, I know it sounds insincere when people say that, but...
/lˈʊk a‍ɪ nˈo‍ʊ ɪt sˈa‍ʊndz ˌɪnsɪnsˈɪ‍ɹ wɛn pˈiːpə‍l sˈe‍ɪ ðˈæt bˈʌt/

405
00:18:44,526 --> 00:18:45,638
we could.
/wiː kˈʊd/

406
00:18:46,474 --> 00:18:47,964
I don't know, Robin.
/a‍ɪ dˈo‍ʊnt nˈo‍ʊ ɹˈɑːbɪn/

407
00:18:48,133 --> 00:18:49,853
I've made such a jackass of myself here.
/a‍ɪv mˌe‍ɪd sˈʌt‍ʃ ɐ d‍ʒˈækæs ʌv ma‍ɪsˈɛlf hˈɪ‍ɹ/

408
00:18:49,914 --> 00:18:54,200
We start hanging out, every time I see you it'll be like, "Oh, that's right. I'm a jackass."
/wiː stˈɑː‍ɹt hˈæŋɪŋ ˈa‍ʊt ˈɛvɹi tˈa‍ɪm a‍ɪ sˈiː juː ˌɪɾə‍l biː lˈa‍ɪk ˈo‍ʊ ðæts ɹˈa‍ɪt a‍ɪm ɐ d‍ʒˈækæs/

409
00:18:54,609 --> 00:18:55,950
You're not a jackass.
/jʊ‍ɹ nˌɑːɾə d‍ʒˈækæs/

410
00:18:56,591 --> 00:18:58,879
Look, I'm sorry. I only moved here in April
/lˈʊk a‍ɪm sˈɔːɹi a‍ɪ ˈo‍ʊnli mˈuːvd hˈɪɹ ɪn ˈe‍ɪpɹə‍l/

411
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,455
and I'm always working and
/ænd a‍ɪm ˈɔːlwe‍ɪz wˈɜːkɪŋ ænd/

412
